<title>EGYPT: Egyptian inflation down to 4.9 pct in May.</title>
<headline>Egyptian inflation down to 4.9 pct in May.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egyptian year-on-year inflation fell to 4.9 percent in May, from 5.4 percent in April and 8.1 percent in May 1996, according to figures from the government's statistics office, available on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The consumer price index for urban areas, set at a base of 100 in the financial year 1986/7, rose 0.52 percent in May, to 383.0 from 381.0 in April 1997, they said. The index stood at 365.2 at the end of May 1996.</p>
<p>				     May 1997   April 1997   May 1996</p>
<p>    Month-on-month		 +0.52	 +0.61	 +1.00</p>
<p>    Year-on-year		   +4.9	  +5.4	  +8.1</p>
<p>    INDEX (base 1986/7)	 383.0	 381.0	 365.2</p>
<p>-- Jonathan Wright +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
